{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/37839","id":4435036826,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABCFlKmg","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37839","diff_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37839.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37839.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/37839","number":37839,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Fix] Prevalidate JSON Schema support per grammar backend","user":{"login":"JustinPerlman","id":69224148,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MjI0MTQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69224148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman","html_url":"https://github.com/JustinPerlman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinPerlman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\n\nSGLang currently treats successful grammar compilation as proof that a JSON Schema is supported. Some backends instead compile successfully while silently dropping constraints:\n\n- XGrammar ignores unsupported assertion keywords and prioritizes `format` over `pattern` over `minLength`/`maxLength`.\n- Outlines Core 0.1.x similarly ignores unsupported assertions and chooses one constraint family based on parser dispatch order.\n\nThe request then succeeds, but generated output can violate the schema the client supplied.\n\n## Change\n\n- Prevalidate JSON Schemas against the configured grammar backend before compilation.\n- Reject XGrammar keywords and string-constraint combinations that XGrammar 0.2.x cannot fully enforce.\n- Reject Outlines constraints and combinations that Outlines Core 0.1.x silently ignores or weakens.\n- Traverse only actual subschema positions, so schema-shaped values inside `const`, `enum`, `default`, and `examples` are not misclassified.\n- Include a JSON Pointer in errors to identify the unsupported nested subschema.\n- Keep each backend native compiler as the final authority for malformed schemas and explicitly unsupported syntax.\n\nRejected schemas use the existing `InvalidGrammarObject` path, which terminates the request as an HTTP 400 instead of generating against a weakened grammar. llguidance is unchanged because its native JSON Schema conversion and matcher construction already reject unsupported input.\n\nThis does not introduce an automatic backend-selection mode; validation follows the backend selected at server launch.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds CPU tests for supported schemas, every known silently ignored XGrammar keyword, unknown formats, mixed string constraints, Outlines semantic-loss cases, safe nested traversal, JSON Pointer escaping, and rejection before backend compilation.\n\nRelated: #28804, #37707, #37726, mlc-ai/xgrammar#798.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #34370738914](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34370738914)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #34370738418](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34370738418)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #34370738639](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34370738639)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->","created_at":"2026-09-03T16:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T05:13:36Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3af952528cda91cdd192166103563580b7849eec","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"DarkSharpness","id":76582120,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NTgyMTIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76582120?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness","html_url":"https://github.com/DarkSharpness","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkSharpness/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"JustinTong0323","id":115166877,"node_id":"U_kgDOBt1OnQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115166877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323","html_url":"https://github.com/JustinTong0323","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JustinTong0323/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ju